Spec clarifications for datagate: the five sentences whose hidden-test reading
Opus 5 gets wrong every time (v7 run, 14 of 14 misses; blind judge 195/200,
see notes/ambiguity-judge.md). Each hunk changes one sentence, and each is
worded to match what the hidden tests and the reference solution do, not to
change the required behaviour.

  checkpoint_1  T22  "detect encoding" -> a fixed UTF-8 / latin-1 ladder
  checkpoint_2  T27  rowid counts the header as row 1
  checkpoint_4  T56  /upload honours the charset query parameter
  checkpoint_4  T63  charset is ignored, not validated, for spreadsheets
  checkpoint_5  T74  a value-bearing force is 400 (drop "additional")

Apply to a copy of the problem, never to the cache in place:

  cp -r ~/.cache/scbench/problems/datagate <root>/datagate
  patch -p1 -d <root> < configs/specs/datagate-clarified.patch

then run with SCBENCH_PROBLEMS_PATH=<root> so the catalog reads the copy. Any run against
this copy is a spec-clarification experiment, not a benchmark score.

